<title>ITALY: Fiat's Caffaro H1 pre-tax profit jumps.</title>
<headline>Fiat's Caffaro H1 pre-tax profit jumps.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1996-09-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Group six months ended June 30</p>
<p>(In billion lire unless stated)</p>
<p>    Cons turnover			  575.2  (up 18 percent)</p>
<p>    Operating result		     43.6   (up 18.2 percent)</p>
<p>    Pre-tax result			 38.1   vs 27.8</p>
<p>    Parent net turnover		  95.4   vs 112.5</p>
<p>    Parent pre-tax result		24.1   vs 4.7</p>
<p>Note - Caffaro is the main chemical operation of Fiat unit Raggrupamento Chimico di Snia Bpd. It said in a statement group first half performance was boosted by the recent acquisition of Siapa.</p>
<p>Caffaro SpA said it estimated second-half results would follow the first-half's positive trend and that 1996 results should outstrip those of 1995 despite difficult exchange and market conditions.</p>
<p>-- Rome newsroom +396 678 2501</p>
</text>
